ery column across the tables, while allowing for heterogeneous representations. Prices appear in different currencies and with different semantics (asking/list price vs selling price vs present price), so separate attributes are kept for asking_price, selling_price, and present_price plus corresponding currency fields. Some tables provide only a generic identifier named id (Tables 9\u201310) rather than listing_id, so source_record_id is included to preserve completeness without forcing an incorrect join key assumption. Unstructured title/name fields (full_title/vehicle_name) are preserved as full_title. Odometer fields come in km, meters, and embedded strings (e.g., '74155 km', 'm 66286000', '44904000 mtrs'), so odometer_value is captured and an odometer_unit attribute is provided to normalize during ingestion. Table-specific codes for fuel/transmission are mapped to the canonical attributes and can be standardized in ETL (e.g., P/D/CNG; M/A; Manual/Automatic). Seller type appears only once (Table 1) and is included to ensure completeness."}, "time": 21.784552600001916}}